DAWNSHORE (The Anchor of the Sun)
Darkling & Darkforme TaxaWith the ontological dysfunction dying out at the border, the dark ecology here is forced to perfectly mimic the raw, brutal reality of mundane terrestrial and coastal wildlife to survive. They are the apex predators of the delta and the star-wood, hiding their shadowy nature beneath mud, shells, and a mimicry of natural forms to avoid the burning, normalized sunlight.
Darkling-Shell-Skitterer (CR 1/4): Small Abomination, Scavenging Evil An opportunistic, hermit-crab or raccoon-like darkling that scours the beaches of the Westersea Bay. Highly vulnerable to the normalized sunlight of Dawnshore, these creatures cram their shadowy, amorphous bodies into discarded giant clam shells, hollowed driftwood, or even discarded packing crates. They scurry out at night to steal fishing supplies, shiny baubles, and rations from the stilt-villages.
Darkling-Silt-Hound (CR 1): Medium Abomination, Pack Evil Mimicking the form of a gaunt, marsh-dwelling coyote or wild dog, these darklings hunt in coordinated packs through the muddy river delta. To protect their sensitive shadow-forms from the sun, they constantly roll in the thick, grey clay of the meltwater rivers. They use the tall coastal reeds to herd wading fishers or Delta Rangers into deep mud-traps before striking.
Darkforme-Star-Shrike (CR 3): Medium Abomination, Plunging Evil A terrifying, avian darkforme that has claimed the high branches of the Astrum Canopy. It perfectly mimics the silhouette of a massive owl or falcon, but its feathers are composed of razor-thin, hardened shadow-glass. It utilizes the dense, geometric canopy of the star-shaped forest to block the sun, waiting in the darkest branches before dropping silently to impale unsuspecting prey on its sharp, metallic-like talons.
Darkforme-Bramble-Stag (CR 5): Large Abomination, Territorial Evil The undisputed shadow-monarch of the terrestrial delta. This creature mimics a colossal, imposing elk or moose that roams the deepest, most serene heart of the Astrum Canopy. Its body is woven from thick, muscular shadow-roots, and its massive antlers are a fractal spread of jagged obsidian. Unlike the chaotic beasts of the inner plains, the Bramble-Stag is terrifyingly calm and calculated, aggressively defending its territory in the star-wood from any Delta Rangers attempting to push the dark ecology back into the wastes.


MARISTANNIO (The Scavenger's Dreadnought)
Darkling & Darkforme Taxa In the deepest, forgotten bilge-levels and abandoned maintenance shafts of the mechanized island, the dark ecology feeds not on psychic despair, but on industrial rot, toxic runoff, and discarded mechanics.
Darkling-Petro-Legion (CR 3): [Large Ooze, Polluted Evil] A vile, localized mutation of the standard Liquid Legion. Formed entirely from pooling Petrodistillate, alchemical runoff, and darkling ooze in the lowest gutters of the city. It is highly flammable, suffocating, and moves as a sentient, corrosive oil-slick that clogs the city's vital gears.
Darkforged-Slag-Brute (CR 1): [Medium Construct, Rusted Evil] Heavily corroded Warforged chassis that were thought to be fully salvaged and discarded into the dark holds. Reanimated by ambient dark magic, these lumbering, water-logged constructs blindly carry out ancient guard protocols, attacking any scavenger unfortunate enough to wander into their forgotten sectors.
Darkling-Grease-Mite (CR 1/4): [Tiny Abomination, Sabotaging Evil] Spider-like darklings that feed explicitly on the lubricants and magical grease of Maristannio's infrastructure. They do little physical damage but excel at dropping down to magically unfasten the tapes and seals of heavily padded mechanics.

NIOLANTEA (The Fungal Spire-Kingdom)
Darkling & Darkforme Taxa The sheer volume of untamed, elder magic required to grow the Colossal Spores has created a terrifying opportunity for the dark ecology. Here, Darklings do not merely exist alongside the flora; they actively seek terrifying, parasitic symbiosis with it.
Darkling-Spore-Symbiote (CR 1): [Small Abomination, Parasitic Evil] A sludge-like darkling that infects the root systems of dead or dying Mycos-Architecture. Once inside, it puppeteers the hollowed fungal stalks, using them as heavily armored, wooden mech-suits to ambush the Seimei and fae-kin.
Darkforme-Strangleweed (CR 3): [Large Abomination, Invasive Evil] A botanical nightmare where thick, grasping shadow-ooze has perfectly mimicked the local iron-vines. It emits a false bioluminescence to lure in wild-shaping druids before wrapping them in an unbreakable, necrotic constriction.
Darkforme-Rot-Blossom (CR 5): [Large Abomination, Decaying Evil] A corrupted, massive flower born from a Darkforme merging with a hyper-fertile seed pod. It sits perfectly still in the canopy, exhaling a localized "Pink Fog" of hallucinogenic, necrotic pollen that causes extreme lethargy and loss of continence control in its victims before it strikes.

HERALDIA (The Arcokingdom)
Darkling & Darkforme Taxa The darkformes that haunt the isolated, sealed-off wings of Heraldia's vertical arcology are not natural evolutions. They are the shameful, locked-away mistakes of arrogant, ancient Wizard-Kings who believed they could bind and domesticate the darkness for their own aristocratic vanity.
Darkling-Porcelain-Thrall (CR 1): [Medium Abomination, Servile Evil] Bizarre, doll-like constructs made of smooth, cracked porcelain and shadow-ooze. They were created by a past Duchess as "perfect, silent servants," but went feral. They now wander the abandoned mid-spans, aggressively trying to "clean" intruders by dissolving them in acid.
Darkling-Gilded-Husk (CR 2): [Medium Abomination, Vain Evil] Amorphous shadow-oozes that have poured themselves into the discarded, highly ornate, gold-veined armor suits of long-dead Heraldian nobles. They clank through the dark corridors, fighting with a terrifying, albeit clumsy, mimicry of high-class fencing.
Darkforme-Chimeric-Dread (CR 6): [Large Abomination, Arrogant Evil] The ultimate, purposeful abomination of a mad Heraldian King. This creature is a horrifying splice of darkling essence and a noble griffin. It possesses a chaotic, shifting anatomy of feathers, bone, and shadow-glass, aggressively hunting anything that lacks royal blood.

THE HIGH SKIES (Northwest / Stormveil Periphery)
Darkling & Darkforme Taxa These high-altitude predators ride the violent thermals of the World-Seam. They frequently attempt to harry ships crossing the Westersea or dive-bomb the coastline, though they are notoriously incapable of maintaining a presence within Stormveil proper, as the kingdom's conductive lightning-rod defenses instantly incinerate their shadowy forms.
Darkling-Gale-Harrier (CR 1/2): [Small Abomination, Plunging Evil] Swarms of jagged, aerodynamic darklings that mimic the silhouettes of seabirds. They dive-bomb from the cloud cover to snatch loose gear or unbalance sailors. While terrifying in the open air, a single strike from Stormveil's ambient electro-defenses turns them to falling ash.
Darkforme-Nimbus-Ray (CR 4): [Large Abomination, Gliding Evil] A massive, manta-like entity of flattened shadow that glides silently on the high-altitude thermals. It attempts to drop directly on top of small skiffs in the Westersea, wrapping the entire vessel in darkness to consume the crew.
Darkforme-Thunderhead (CR 7): [Huge Abomination, Atmospheric Evil] A brooding, floating mass of concentrated darkling miasma that attempts to mimic the apocalyptic monsoons of the World-Seam. It generates its own localized, necrotic hail and fierce downdrafts to smash airborne travelers into the ocean. It instinctively avoids the airspace directly above Stormveil, fearing the organized electrical retaliation of the storm-mages.

